day, shouts of a different sort were heard in another part of London. These were not cries

6
00:00:35.181 --> 00:00:44.768
of joy but rather shouts of anger. For on that day, Tom Canty was born into

7
00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:51.521
a very poor family dominated by his boorish father, John. The Cantys lived in a squalid part

8
00:00:51.522 --> 00:00:58.999
of London, in a section known as Offal Court. Their home consisted of just one room with

9
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.586
piles of straw and old blankets thrown about for beds. During the day Tom and his

10
00:01:05.587 --> 00:01:13.586
older twin sisters were sent out to the streets to beg. If Tom returned home empty-handed, his

11
00:01:13.587 --> 00:01:20.903
father would beat him and then send him to bed with nothing to eat. Yet Tom

12
00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:29.484
was not unhappy. He was still a young boy who did not yet know how bad his

13
00:01:29.485 --> 00:01:41.305
circumstances were. And he had a mother and sisters who loved him dearly, and tried to

14
00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:50.973
take care of him despite the abuses of his father. Tom also had a friend in Offal

15
00:01:50.974 --> 00:02:02.104
